{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"d2e8d03e4664f78e6c194bca332dda002c8c52024b52e117e6b3e589979ac655\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    \"Read native schematic and PCB; verified component identities, pin/net assignments and saved population flags.\",\n    \"Fresh KiCad 10.0.7 netlist export matches supplied component population and connectivity.\",\n    \"Calculated fitted-resistor connectivity and R1 pad separation.\",\n    \"Inspected supplied ERC, DRC, netlist and geometry reports and execution records. ERC/DRC report zero native violations; these results do not establish assembled electrical conduction.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"defect\",\n      \"condition\": \"Assembly follows the saved population, with no alternate assembly override.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Line 1: requires a fitted resistive DC path from /IN to /OUT\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/requirements.txt\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 1252–1285: Device:R instance R1, value 10k, has (dnp yes)\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Line 304: (attr smd dnp); lines 359–374: separate R1 pads assigned /IN and /OUT\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"components/comp[@ref='R1']/property[@name='dnp']; nets/net[@name='/IN'] and nets/net[@name='/OUT']\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/design.xml\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 138–154: only resistor is DNP; fitted_resistor_edges is empty; fitted_resistive_path_IN_to_OUT is false; pad gap is 0.8 mm\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/circuit/experiments/population_result.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"id\": \"circuit-001\",\n      \"location\": \"R1, between /IN and /OUT\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"The only resistor connecting the two nets is excluded from assembly. Its separate PCB pads and terminating tracks do not conduct across the absent component.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Both native files mark R1 DNP, corroborated by the supplied and freshly exported netlists. The remaining fitted parts are connector J1 and capacitor C1 from /OUT to GND; neither supplies the missing resistive connection. The saved assembly therefore fails the stated DC-path requirement, despite clean ERC and DRC results.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"DNP R1 removes the required fitted resistive path\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"No physical assembly measurements or SPICE simulation performed; the finding follows directly from saved population and topology.\",\n    \"Voltage, load, ratings, tolerances, startup, shutdown, reset, brownout and interface behavior were not evaluated because corresponding operating conditions are unspecified.\",\n    \"ERC/DRC were inspected rather than rerun; their listed ignored checks remain untested. Saved zone fill was not regenerated, and no comprehensive independent clearance audit was performed.\",\n    \"Geometry extraction emitted PROPERTY_ENUM assertions. Relevant population and pad data were independently corroborated from native files.\",\n    \"Commands, versions, assumptions, calculations and outcomes are recorded in review-work/circuit/experiments/check_population.py, commands.json, supplied_check_records.json and notes.md.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"abf747f43b1f5560fc5a55fc37b47a8eafa2918138621185161442af2f48582a\",\n  \"role\": \"circuit\",\n  \"run_id\": \"e1ba1d6d-cc99-4b33-b937-6f924ac41853\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
